{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "game": "hsr",
  "id": "journey-of-the-moles-belobog-ancient-poetry-collection",
  "name": "Journey of the Moles — Belobog Ancient Poetry Collection",
  "sourceUrl": "https://honkai-star-rail.fandom.com/wiki/Journey_of_the_Moles_%E2%80%94_Belobog_Ancient_Poetry_Collection",
  "scrapedAt": "2026-08-02T09:05:40.465Z",
  "volumes": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "volumeKey": "pilgrimage-north-of-snowfield",
      "label": "Pilgrimage North of Snowfield",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I had once gazed toward the snowcapped peak"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ceb398de129afb61"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Frosty springs had yet flow into the prologue"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But appear skybound the eyes of others in the dark hours"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Clouds enveloped the mason in the village"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And travelers peer into the Amber's past"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-77c568a26df57cc5"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The journey of my heart"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Is the pilgrimage of my soul"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-deb4e0692460cb91"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I had once gazed toward the snowcapped peak"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ceb398de129afb61-2"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "In the days boreas borrowed my singing voice"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The land and the birds will all fall silent"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "You will see the spine of the world on the mining veins"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Above the stars and below the bonfire wood"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Forging memories in the name of the blacksmith"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Given meaning by the supreme fire"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-a370919f61d5a64c"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I dig burrows, and you build walls"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I dig burrows, and you build walls"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And one day the walls will fall"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And one day the tears will fall"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The end is etched into the distant plains"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Waiting for this poem to die"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Till the snowcapped peaks close their eyes"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Or the flowers fall"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c57d2fca17c83a82"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "volumeKey": "dusk-in-rivet-town",
      "label": "Dusk in Rivet Town",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I am jealous of the gear that lost the dusk"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The turning days never had a future"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Three shields per bottle"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The retail sale of souls"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Just enough for one mouthful in a meal"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-d7d72591bf96b85a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Amber, amber, yet another amber for enrichment"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The stars in the hometown are never on time"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Wind, wind, another wind howls as a hawk"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The evening light tolls"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And takes away the stone pier with nowhere to go in Rivet Town"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-20901beb772e49f5"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Shackles applied, on a moist heart"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "How could it be measured in kilograms"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yet another stone statue stands at the start of the mine shaft"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The mining machines sculpt the pattern of its own trousers"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Passersby all say"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "It's so foolish"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-fb05b3e1501854f6"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "volumeKey": "chubby-larry",
      "label": "Chubby Larry",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Chubby Larry walking one step every three seconds"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "To cross his brown kingdom"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Past the"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Forty centimeters of mine cart"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Past the"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Festival that lasts from winter to summer"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-09f1b739396df7e7"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Qlipoth had said"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "We should build his temple with love"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But humans only ever offered rocks and words"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-c6789b3375f7d1f4"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Qlipoth had been here"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And gave him a sexy pickaxe"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He thought it was a secret"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He always faced the night deep in the mines, and shouted with his arms up high"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Chubby Larry!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He thought he probably wasn't young anymore"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fifty years of song"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sealed away his arms like a mine collapse"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-cadfb6b00235aa1a"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Larry of the Broken-Arms!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He embraced the winter like a rock crab and roared"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He walked past the silent beach of broken rocks with his draft"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "His boss always scolded him"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "With a ring of glory! With the clouds!"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-4adf01c011d244ec"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Lazy Larry!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He stared at the funeral worm at the corner"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And cried in front of them, alone"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Larry the Crybaby!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "People no longer needed his stories"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Using the wanted poster of poverty as silver threads, they sewed his mouth shut"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-9198c7d51760e72d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sorrowful Larry!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "But he could still hear"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The breaths of flowing ores and the running steps of words"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Sorrowful Larry had to live in a portable coffin"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Taking out his sincere pickaxe"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Folding it into the form of birds he had never seen"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And flipped backward twice in overcritical degrees"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-0f50ce194346723f"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Mute Larry!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Weaving lyrics in the caves all on his own"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He ate seventeen, Soothing Mushrooms"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "He said, \"Wake me!\""
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "And seventeen poets slapped his face"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-e11c95041bd02756"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They say, Larry was no more!"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Larry had nothing and crossed the Great Mine"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Like an iron pickaxe, he was buried in the earth"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-22df87b97c81d79d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The passersby never saw this"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "They just say"
              },
              {
                "type": "br"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A chubby man fell asleep"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-96971e7e5328c3e0"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
